      "problem": "Find the root of $f(x)=\\sqrt[4]{5x+16}-3.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[4]{5x+16}-3=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{5x+16}-3 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{5x+16} & =3 \\\\ (\\sqrt[4]{5x+16})^{4} & ={3}^{4} \\\\ 5x+16 & =81 \\\\ 5x & =65 \\\\ x & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we must check the answer by substituting it back into the initial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{5\\cdot 13+16}-3 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{81}-3 & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=13.$",
