      "problem": "Find the root of $f(x)=-3\\sqrt[7]{8x+11}+3.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n-3\\sqrt[7]{8x+11}+3=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3\\sqrt[7]{8x+11}+3 & =0 \\\\ -3\\sqrt[7]{8x+11} & =-3 \\\\ \\sqrt[7]{8x+11} & =1 \\\\ (\\sqrt[7]{8x+11})^{7} & ={1}^{7} \\\\ 8x+11 & =1 \\\\ 8x & =-10 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=-\\frac{5}{4}.$",
